# Alice Hotel — Backend

Base package: `com.alice.hotel.api`. Java **17**. Context path `/api/v1`.

## Feature layout

- Controllers / services: `domain/{admin|system|common}/{feature}/web|service|impl`
- DTOs: `dto/{admin|system|common}/{feature}/` (`*DTO`, `*SearchDTO`, `*RequestDTO`, `*ResponseDTO`)
- Persistence: `entity/`, `repository/` (`*Entity`, `*Repository`)
- Template: `domain/admin/hotelRoom/`

## API rules

- Controllers return `ApiResponse<T>` only — never raw JPA entities
- Business errors: throw `CustomException` with `ApiStatus`; rely on `GlobalExceptionHandler`
- New admin resources: `@RequestMapping("/a/{kebab-resource}")` with REST:
  - `POST .../list`, `GET .../{id}`, `POST`, `PUT .../{id}`, `DELETE .../{id}`
- Public: `/auth/**`, `/files/**`

## Build / deploy

- Local: Gradle / IDE `Application`
- Release artifact: `bootWar` → `ALICE_HOTEL_ROOT.war`
- Do not add new hardcoded secrets in `application.properties` committed to git

See [STANDARDS.md](../../STANDARDS.md) §2 and §5.
